E=[
(G1,102,r'''Jesus isn't demanding sinless performance, which is impossible in this life.''',r'''Jesus isn't demanding sinless performance. Apart from Christ and His Mother, no one old enough to know right from wrong lives without any sin at all (cf. Council of Trent, Session VI, canon 23). If "perfect" meant a flawless record, the command would be impossible, and all we could do is trust God to look past our failures. That is not what He asked.'''),
(G2,141,r'''the marriage vows when two become one flesh;''',r'''the marriage vows, when two give themselves to each other for life;'''),
(G3,163,r'''"I am the living bread which came down from heaven; if any one eats of this bread, he will live for ever." (John 6:51). Christ gives''',r'''"For my flesh is food indeed, and my blood is drink indeed." (John 6:55). Christ gives'''),
(G4,197,r'''Like Mary at the Annunciation—"the Holy Spirit will come upon you, and the power of the Most High will overshadow you" (Luke 1:35)—we come''',r'''Like Mary at the Annunciation—"And the angel said to her, 'The Holy Spirit will come upon you, and the power of the Most High will overshadow you; therefore the child to be born will be called holy, the Son of God.'" (Luke 1:35)—we come'''),
(G4,197,r'''That drop adds nothing to the chalice.''',r'''That drop is real, but beside the infinite love it joins, it is almost nothing.'''),
(G4,197,r'''And that is all love ever asks of us—not to add to His gift, but to let Him fill us.''',r'''And that is all love ever asks of us: to receive His gift of love and let it fill us.'''),
(G5,213,r'''"Truly, truly, I say to you, unless you eat the flesh of the Son of man and drink his blood, you have no life in you" (John 6:53).''',r'''"So Jesus said to them, 'Truly, truly, I say to you, unless you eat the flesh of the Son of man and drink his blood, you have no life in you;'" (John 6:53).'''),
(G6,262,r'''without the woman whose *Fiat* opened the door to all of it. *"Behold, I am the handmaid of the Lord; let it be to me according to your word"* (Luke 1:38) — and the Word became flesh in her womb.''',r'''without Our Lady, the Blessed Virgin Mary, whose *Fiat* opened the door to all of it (cf. Luke 1:38, quoted in Chapter 9): at her yes, the Word became flesh in her womb.'''),
(G6,262,r'''when nearly every apostle had fled — *"standing by the cross of Jesus were his mother…"* (John 19:25). There''',r'''when nearly every apostle had fled (cf. John 19:25). There'''),
(G6,262,r'''to the whole Church: *"Behold, your mother"* (John 19:27).''',r'''to the whole Church: *"Then he said to the disciple, 'Behold, your mother!' And from that hour the disciple took her to his own home."* (John 19:27).'''),
(G7,288,r'''"that they may all be one; even as thou, Father, art in me, and I in thee, that they also may be in us" (John 17:21).''',r'''"that they may all be one; even as thou, Father, art in me, and I in thee, that they also may be in us, so that the world may believe that thou hast sent me" (John 17:21).'''),
(G7,288,r'''As St. Paul writes, there is "one body and one Spirit... one Lord, one faith, one baptism, one God and Father of all" (Ephesians 4:4-6)—the unity of the Church''',r'''As St. Paul writes: "There is one body and one Spirit, just as you were called to the one hope that belongs to your call, one Lord, one faith, one baptism, one God and Father of us all, who is above all and through all and in all" (Ephesians 4:4-6). The unity of the Church'''),
(G8,316,r'''Every Christian division is a scandal that contradicts the Gospel. Christ established one Church where He granted His authority to teach everything He had commanded: "All authority in heaven and on earth has been given to me. Go therefore and make disciples of all nations... teaching them to observe all that I have commanded you" (Matthew 28:18-20).''',r'''The Church does not soften it: division among Christians "openly contradicts the will of Christ, scandalizes the world, and damages the holy cause of preaching the Gospel to every creature" (Second Vatican Council, *Unitatis Redintegratio* 1). Christ established one Church and granted her His authority to teach everything He had commanded: "And Jesus came and said to them, 'All authority in heaven and on earth has been given to me. Go therefore and make disciples of all nations, baptizing them in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, teaching them to observe all that I have commanded you; and lo, I am with you always, to the close of the age.'" (Matthew 28:18-20).'''),
]
